                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "DOESN\"T WORK ON THE STEAM FRAME\n\nSo I'll start off by saying, At least before and on release it was a fun game. I played it on the Index and it worked fine. Fun game but haven't played since official release.\n\nI went to play this today (9/29/26) on the Steam Frame and couldn't play it. I'm not sure if it was because of standalone mode or not, but it wasn't seeing my controllers at all, couldn't get past the title screen.  So far this is the only game that I've tried on it that has had this issue, so it might just not like it, I will have to try from my computer later on when I have more time.\n\n\nAlso it seems like this game has pretty much been abandoned after release with no new updates coming out after.\n\nI will update this review if i get it working on the Frame. \n\n\nBut in it's current state and the face that I couldn't even play it (at least in standalone mode) I can't recommended this game, even though on the index I did have fun, but no updates, since pretty much release date and no communication from the devs means i can't recommend this game.\n\nUpdate:\n\nI still couldn't play it streaming from my PC this game DOESN\"T WORK ON THE STEAM FRAME",
